# The app's own pages all load index.html; anything else that doesn't exist is a real 404
# (public/404.html). Without these rules Pages answered every missing file with index.html and a
# 200, and during a deploy a script fetched before it arrived got HTML that the edge then cached.
/host           /  200
/host/*         /  200
/play/*         /  200
/report/*       /  200
